{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Table 1.} The benchmarked methods: model family ({\i tier}), the engine each one actually runs, whether it can decline to call a cell ({\i rejection}), and the runtime stack it was run on; each has its own pinned environment (\u167 ?2.5). Bold marks the methods added to this panel here.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8224 ? {\f1 linear-anova-pca} has no method paper: it is a baseline assembled here from scikit-learn components, tuned deliberately to be the strongest simple competitor we could build (\u167 ?1).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Eleven of the thirteen are trained on each dataset\u8217's own reference} and run the full accuracy/cost matrix of \u167 ?3.1 on all six datasets, so none is compared on a favorable subset. The remaining two are {\b pretrained annotators with fixed label vocabularies}, which changes what can be measured rather than excusing them from measurement:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b scPRINT} is a zero-shot foundation model over a fixed {\b Cell Ontology (CL)} vocabulary \u8212- CL being the standard controlled vocabulary of cell types, used throughout as the common ground between datasets that name the same cell differently; it cannot emit labels outside that set and skips symbol-keyed datasets.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Pan-human Azimuth} ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.07.16.738997"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
[Sarkar et al.\u160 ?2026]
}}}
) is a supervised hierarchical classifier over a single organism-wide typology \u8212- 8 levels, 382 leaves, ~7M parameters, a fixed 5,055-gene panel, trained on 9.7M curated cells, with abstention {\i learned rather than thresholded} \u8212- the model is trained to answer {\f1 Unassigned}, instead of having a probability cutoff applied to its output afterwards. It is the closest published counterpart to this paper\u8217's broad pass, and the teacher we distill in \u167 ?3.4.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Neither predicts into the dataset\u8217's label strings, so {\b exact-match accuracy against those strings is a vocabulary artifact, not an accuracy signal} \u8212- {\f1 regulatory T cell} \u8594 ? {\f1 Treg cell} and {\f1 non-classical monocyte} \u8594 ? {\f1 CD16 monocyte} are correct answers that score zero. Both are therefore scored {\b ontology-only} (\u167 ?2.4) and reported in their own block in \u167 ?3.1, on the three datasets where reference and query both carry Cell Ontology ids. They appear again in \u167 ?3.6 (foundation-model zero-shot) and \u167 ?3.4 (Azimuth as broad pass, and as distillation teacher).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b scPred} is excluded outright: unmaintained; it requires harmony\u8217's removed {\f1 HarmonyMatrix} API and older harmony versions do not compile on the current toolchain.\par}
